{"diagnosis": "Loopback send of 0xa5 at divider 64 never sets recv_buf_valid, so reg_dat_do never returns the byte and sim traps uart timeout after 22023 cycles vs expected RX. TX dummy logic quickly restores ser_tx to idle-high, so reset value is not fatal. Root cause is recv_state declared as reg [3:1] (3-bit, max 7) instead of [3:0], so states 8-10 are unreachable and receive never completes.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -39,5 +39,5 @@
-	reg [3:1] recv_state;
+	reg [3:0] recv_state;
 	reg [31:0] recv_divcnt;
 	reg [7:0] recv_pattern;
 	reg [7:0] recv_buf_data;
 	reg recv_buf_valid;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (0x1) with loopback byte 0xa5 received, no uart timeout"}

